'''Robert Earnest Rozier Jr.''' (born July 28, 1955) is an American [[murder in United States law|murderer]] and former professional [[defensive end]] in [[gridiron football]].

Born in Alaska and raised in California, Rozier was a high-school and collegiate athlete before briefly playing professional [[gridiron football]].  In the 1980s, he joined the [[Nation of Yahweh]], and by Halloween 1986 had killed at least four people on behalf of the religious group.  Charged therefor, Rozier [[turn state's evidence|turned state's evidence]] against the group and [[Yahweh ben Yahweh|its leader]], and was sentenced to 22 years in prison; he was [[parole]]d after ten and put into [[United States Federal Witness Protection Program|witness protection]].  After Rozier was caught [[dishonoured cheque|bouncing checks]] in 1999, he was sentenced to [[life imprisonment in the United States|25 years-to-life]] under California's [[three-strikes law]] in 2001.

